```

### Important

- **Do not ignore source code**, grammar files, documentation, test cases, parser tables, or project configuration.
- Generated compiler outputs (AST, TAC, IR, assembly, etc.) will not be committed by default.
- `.env.example` is allowed to be committed so others can configure the project.
- `.agents/skills/` is intentionally **not ignored**, so your installed Antigravity skills can be tracked by Git if you want.

If you want, I can also write the **initial project folder structure** for your Compiler Construction project so Antigravity follows a clean architecture from the beginning.